# Review follow-ups (Opus review of d260b78..20d459b)
## dynamic_reader.zig (do after task 2.5 lands, with the D1 streaming iterator work)
- any_nested (≈:612-617) loops over ALL top-level columns; should loop over col_indices (requested columns) AND fillFlatRow must then index column_values via top_infos[idx].leaf_start, not the top index. Changing only the loop would read wrong columns. Drop the redundant `num_leaf_columns == num_top` check (≈:678). Fix the comment/commit wording.
- errdefer page_result.deinit(self.allocator) after the page decode call in both V1 (≈:930-946) and V2 (≈:989-1005) branches; null each field once ownership moves. Pre-existing leak on OOM in appendSlice.
- Make sure 2.5's iterator test goes through the rows_arena branch of assembleFlatRows under std.testing.allocator.
## column_writer.zig (bundle into task 3.5)
- Golden-bytes test never triggers the fallback: add a case with a small dictionary_size_limit (e.g. 4000 for ints_distinct, 100 for strings) asserting bytes == the PLAIN writer's output for the same input, and no leaks.
## column_decoder.zig + rle.zig (free now)
- column_decoder.zig ≈:1652/:1680: `data_offset + len > value_data.len` can overflow on 32-bit; write `if (len > value_data.len - data_offset) return error.EndOfData;`.
- rle.zig ≈:115 bitPackedSize: num_values * bit_width unchecked; use std.math.mul and return an error.
- decodeFlatPlainFixed: skip def_mask alloc when max_def_level == 0; add INT32/FLOAT test and a bit-packed-levels test.
